<title>INDIA: Indian Shipping -- Cochin cargoes - Nov 14.</title>
<headline>Indian Shipping -- Cochin cargoes - Nov 14.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the berthing schedule of major vessels loading and unloading at India's Cochin port on November 14:</p>
<p> Commodity	    Tons	    Ship		     Berthing</p>
<p>		     (LDD/ULD)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Urea		 23,000 (ULD)     Ionian Coral	   20/10</p>
<p>Zinc</p>
<p> Concentrate     13,000 (ULD)     Alan Peg		 10/11</p>
<p>Crude		41,000 (ULD)     Tagore		   13/11</p>
<p>Muriate of</p>
<p> Potash	     8,000 (ULD)     Mali II		  12/11</p>
<p>Sulphur	    10,000 (ULD)     Guardian Angel	 13/11</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>		  Note:</p>
<p>	    LDD - Loading</p>
<p>	    ULD - Unloading</p>
<p>	   (Source: J.M.Baxi &amp; Co, Cochin)</p>
<p>Lloyds Shipping adds:</p>
<p>Cochin - four vessels due, up to 1 days delay expected, 4 vessels loading at berth, 7 discharging at berth, 1 waiting at anchorage, 2 vessels in shipyard drydock.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
